{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time","id":1451129,"title":"the relations of Flux and Time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-06T06:36:37-07:00","id":1451129,"title":"the relations of Flux and Time","content":"I never understood what Flux has to do with Time.<br /> It's very clear to me the relation of Flux and the alternate universes of the Continuum... but Time???<br /> <br /> 1) Why would Flux enable Mercer to travel through time?<br /> 2) Can he &quot;control Time&quot; locally, too? I mean, 2.1) speed up or slow down things?; 2.2) Age or de-age things?<br /> <br /> \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:24:22-07:00","id":1451134,"title":"","content":"First of all, it's not alternate universes; it's alternate timelines. That is, the most common usage of flux is to reach sideways in time. Max has the additional ability to reach forward or backward in time. And yes, he is demonstrably able to manipulate the flow of time. I forget whether the new edition includes the same fiction; but the opening fiction from the first edition of the game included hey scene where Max sped up time for himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T08:17:40-07:00","id":1451143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451134#post1451134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, it's not alternate universes; it's alternate timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate this, please? I always thought Trinity Continuum was about a Multiverse, not &quot;alternate timelines&quot;...please, explain a little more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451134#post1451134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, he is demonstrably able to manipulate the flow of time. I forget whether the new edition includes the same fiction; but the opening fiction from the first edition of the game included hey scene where Max sped up time for himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I'm also from 1st edition (sometimes I feel like a dinosaur XD), and I also remember the sidebar that says that Mercer could speed &amp; &quot;unspeed&quot; things in 1st edition... I'm curious to know if this is also true in 2nd edition, I mean, what Max can or can't do locally with his time powers?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T09:34:42-07:00","id":1451145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time#post1451129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never understood what Flux has to do with Time.<br /> It's very clear to me the relation of Flux and the alternate universes of the Continuum... but Time???<br /> <br /> 1) Why would Flux enable Mercer to travel through time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flux -- Luck -- is the manipulation of probability, in effect bringing a desired outcome from an adjacent universe in the Continuum and imposing it on your location.<br /> <br /> If you think of the timeline as a line stretching left to right, horizontally along the X-axis, probability is a deflection of this line up or down, along the Y-axis. &quot;Perpendicular time,&quot; in a sense.<br /> <br /> Mercer's unique manipulations are instead along the X-axis, horizontally. He affects &quot;linear time,&quot; or at least his own passage through it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Can he &quot;control Time&quot; locally, too? I mean, 2.1) speed up or slow down things?; 2.2) Age or de-age things?<br /> <br /> \ud83e\udd14 </div> </div> </div>Details of his abilities remain to be described, but it's fairly safe to assume his capabilities are pretty close to what he was able to do in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T09:53:20-07:00","id":1451147,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing as to what you mean by the term Multiverse, so correct me if I'm wrong. A Multiverse is a discrete set of distinct universes. These universes exist side by side; but while the denizens of a given universe can in theory reach out to the other universes and interact with them, the universe's are now and always have been completely and utterly distinct from each other.<br /> <br /> Not so with a Continuum of timelines. First of all, they aren't separate universes; they're the same universe, having developed differently. The same laws of physics apply across the board, and two seemingly distinct timeline were not always so: at some point in the past, there was no way to distinguish them from each other. <br /> <br /> Second: although I have been speaking of them as if they were discrete timelines, they aren't. Point a gun at a Target and squeeze the trigger. The bullet may hit dead center, or it could be off by a few inches in any direction. There aren't one or two possible outcomes; there is an infinitude of them. When you pull the trigger, the Continuum expands to include timelines for all possible outcomes. <br /> <br /> In practice, most of these differences don't matter: who cares if the bullets is off by half an inch in one direction or a quarter of an inch in another direction? So we only look at those cases where the differences matter; and that gives the illusion of discrete universes. <br /> <br /> Ultimately though, it's the branching outcome that distinguishes a timeline based approach from a multiverse. The flow of time is essentially a chain of causes and effect. Thus, the connection between time and the continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T15:14:19-07:00","id":1451171,"title":"","content":"This is really cool.<br /> <br /> I get that they\u2019ll never do this for real, but I still think you could make the World of Darkness one of the alternate timelines in the Trinity Continuum in your homebrew and not violate the fundamental physics of the setting. Maybe make Awakened magick (and by extension linear magic) like a variant form of telluric energy and have it branch off from the core setting somewhere around the dawn of recorded civilization (around 5000 BCE give or take a couple thousand years; archaeology is not my strong point lol).<br /> <br /> Or maybe way earlier like 100,000 BCE when the first Changing Breeds were created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-06-2021, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T23:34:03-07:00","id":1451186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451171#post1451171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still think you could make the World of Darkness one of the alternate timelines in the Trinity Continuum in your homebrew and not violate the fundamental physics of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy enough- you can just have a Quantum 10 Nova make a universe like that (or a perfect simulation of one) as a pet project one day.<br /> <br /> Actually, considering how screwed up the WoD is, probably a heavily corrupted Nova at work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:08:05-07:00","id":1451230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451186#post1451186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easy enough- you can just have a Quantum 10 Nova make a universe like that (or a perfect simulation of one) as a pet project one day.<br /> <br /> Actually, considering how screwed up the WoD is, probably a heavily corrupted Nova at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect \ud83d\ude0a! What year do you think this branch would have split from the main Trinity Continuum (the core setting)? Or would it be an entirely separate and discrete (did I use that right?) universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:09:32-07:00","id":1451231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451147#post1451147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing as to what you mean by the term Multiverse, so correct me if I'm wrong. A Multiverse is a discrete set of distinct universes. These universes exist side by side; but while the denizens of a given universe can in theory reach out to the other universes and interact with them, the universe's are now and always have been completely and utterly distinct from each other. Not so with a Continuum of timelines. First of all, they aren't separate universes; they're the same universe, having developed differently. The same laws of physics apply across the board, and two seemingly distinct timeline were not always so: at some point in the past, there was no way to distinguish them from each other.(...) Ultimately though, it's the branching outcome that distinguishes a timeline based approach from a multiverse. The flow of time is essentially a chain of causes and effect. Thus, the connection between time and the continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your definitions, and mostly agree with them. That said...<br /> <br /> 1) I always thought that both kinds (timelines and universes) exist in the Trinity Continuum. And it's &quot;natural state&quot; is a multiverse; alternate timelines only occur if a time traveler changes something. No change in history, no timelines.<br /> <br /> 2) The main reasons is: as far as I know, <i><b>there are </b></i>&quot;universes&quot; with <i>different Physics Laws </i>(eg., some obey the &quot;Four Color&quot; flavor of Aberrant; other ones function with the physics laws of &quot;Deconstruction&quot;, and so on), inside of the Trinity Continuum. Going even further, every &quot;House Ruled universe&quot; is another example (that is, basically most if not all the game worlds of actual players \ud83d\ude05).<br /> <br /> 3) I always thought Dramatic Editing - the most powerful Flux Power for Talents - worked by &quot;sampling&quot; (copy+paste) <i>another universe</i>, not another <i>timeline of his own universe</i>. You see, if I use Dramatic Edit to &quot;create&quot; a door in a house, or any kind of Retcon, I'm sampling from another universe, not another timeline, since the timeline that someone already built the said door doesn't even exist (since no one built it unless I use Dramatic Editing).<br /> <br /> 4) I'd really like to hear what the Devs have to say about these points... does the game world assumes that there are only &quot;universes&quot;, or only &quot;timelines&quot;, or both, or another kind that works differently? (and how does it work?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 06-07-2021, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:54:59-07:00","id":1451237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451186#post1451186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easy enough- you can just have a Quantum 10 Nova make a universe like that (or a perfect simulation of one) as a pet project one day.<br /> <br /> Actually, considering how screwed up the WoD is, probably a heavily corrupted Nova at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. At my table, in the Trinity Continuum a Quantum 10 nova botched the Universe Generation roll, creating a universe hostile to itself. It then created the Primordials as its thought form children who overthrew it, who then built Creation and were over thrown, leading to the end of the Time of Tumult where Creation became the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Purely my head canon, but my long time players get a kick out of linking the three main White Wolf properties and little easter eggs popping up. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T12:06:46-07:00","id":1451239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451237#post1451237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. At my table, in the Trinity Continuum a Quantum 10 nova botched the Universe Generation roll, creating a universe hostile to itself. It then created the Primordials as its thought form children who overthrew it, who then built Creation and were over thrown, leading to the end of the Time of Tumult where Creation became the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Purely my head canon, but my long time players get a kick out of linking the three main White Wolf properties and little easter eggs popping up. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it! You\u2019re named for the Shinto god of war, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T16:34:36-07:00","id":1451266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451231#post1451231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your definitions, and mostly agree with them. That said...<br /> <br /> 1) I always thought that both kinds (timelines and universes) exist in the Trinity Continuum. And it's &quot;natural state&quot; is a multiverse; alternate timelines only occur if a time traveler changes something. No change in history, no timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, my understanding is the exact opposite of this: alternate timelines are spontaneously forming constantly; and Talents tap into them to engage in their \u201cpowers\u201d. No alternate timelines, no Talents. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451231#post1451231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The main reasons is: as far as I know, <i><b>there are </b></i>&quot;universes&quot; with <i>different Physics Laws </i>(eg., some obey the &quot;Four Color&quot; flavor of Aberrant; other ones function with the physics laws of &quot;Deconstruction&quot;, and so on), inside of the Trinity Continuum. Going even further, every &quot;House Ruled universe&quot; is another example (that is, basically most if not all the game worlds of actual players \ud83d\ude05).</div> </div> </div> </div> That notion is, as far as I can tell, something that has only appeared in TC aberrant; and there, only in the form of optional rules that the player group can use to tailor the feel of their game; there's nothing in TC:Ab to suggest that there's any in-game reality to the different rules variants. <br /> <br /> Though I won't say that you can't go there if you want to. For one thing, Quantum abilities are among the most varied in the Continuum: the Superiors, Aberrants, and Sub-Aberrants of TC:\u00c6on bear only a superficial similarity to the Novas of TC:Aberrant or the Stalwarts of TC:Adventure!, suggesting that the way Quantum abilities operate mutates over time; and <i>that</i> means that subtly different versions of the rules for Quantum abilities could potentially exist in different timelines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451231#post1451231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I always thought Dramatic Editing - the most powerful Flux Power for Talents - worked by &quot;sampling&quot; (copy+paste) <i>another universe</i>, not another <i>timeline of his own universe</i>. You see, if I use Dramatic Edit to &quot;create&quot; a door in a house, or any kind of Retcon, I'm sampling from another universe, not another timeline, since the timeline that someone already built the said door doesn't even exist (since no one built it unless I use Dramatic Editing).</div> </div> </div> </div> Different timelines means different sequences of events, but the same rules; different universes means different rules. <br /> <br /> Also, Dramatic Editing never causes something that <i>wasn't</i> there to suddenly appear; it merely causes something that <i>might have been there already</i> to <i>definitely</i> be there. It's a bit like <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schr%C3%B6dinger&#39;s_cat\" target=\"_blank\">Schrodinger's Cat</a>: until someone checks to see if the door is there or not, it's in an indeterminate state where it may or may not be there, as far as the Talent is concerned: one might say that its existence is in Flux. And not only does the Talent get to treat it as being in Flux, he gets to determine (subconsciously) how that Flux will resolve. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451231#post1451231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) I'd really like to hear what the Devs have to say about these points... does the game world assumes that there are only &quot;universes&quot;, or only &quot;timelines&quot;, or both, or another kind that works differently? (and how does it work?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian Watson answered just before I did; and he's the head honcho where the Trinity Continuum is concerned. In a nutshell, he said that it's a timeline thing, with Luck being distortions in a timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T16:57:45-07:00","id":1451269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451237#post1451237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. At my table, in the Trinity Continuum a Quantum 10 nova botched the Universe Generation roll, creating a universe hostile to itself. It then created the Primordials as its thought form children who overthrew it, who then built Creation and were over thrown, leading to the end of the Time of Tumult where Creation became the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Purely my head canon, but my long time players get a kick out of linking the three main White Wolf properties and little easter eggs popping up. .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Malfeas sure has ARMS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T17:12:55-07:00","id":1451270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451237#post1451237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. At my table, in the Trinity Continuum a Quantum 10 nova botched the Universe Generation roll, creating a universe hostile to itself. It then created the Primordials as its thought form children who overthrew it, who then built Creation and were over thrown, leading to the end of the Time of Tumult where Creation became the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Purely my head canon, but my long time players get a kick out of linking the three main White Wolf properties and little easter eggs popping up. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a nitpick: last I checked, Universe Creation isn't a thing in Trinity Continuum. At least, it hasn't been <i>established</i> to be a thing. I seem to recall TC:Ab dialing back a bit on just how gonzo Quantum Powers can get; and the top-tier powers from the original game's player's guide tended to be casualties (along with the mind-reading stuff that got reserved for psiads). Incidentally, another of those likely casualties was time control. <br /> <br /> In <i>my</i> games, universe creation and time manipulation are both uber-Talent things, not Quantum Powers \u2014 though there are no (known) uber-Talents who have achieved the former; and only Max Mercer has achieved the latter (for now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T21:31:26-07:00","id":1451281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451270#post1451270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a nitpick: last I checked, Universe Creation isn't a thing in Trinity Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a thing, it's in the setting secretes for TC: Aeon: &quot;Those that survive become wondrous creatures that can create their own private universes.&quot; (pg. 363) Now, whether a created &quot;private&quot; universe is of the same size as the first... no clue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T01:34:23-07:00","id":1451289,"title":"","content":"Terra Firma, p. 130.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T03:14:43-07:00","id":1451297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451270#post1451270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, another of those likely casualties was time control.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like some degree of Aberrant/Nova time control is still around- the listing of Elemental Themes in Aberrant (p 210) lists Time among the things that could be affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T06:47:11-07:00","id":1451305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1451266#post1451266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, Dramatic Editing never causes something that <i>wasn't</i> there to suddenly appear; it merely causes something that <i>might have been there already</i> to <i>definitely</i> be there. It's a bit like <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schr%C3%B6dinger&#39;s_cat\" target=\"_blank\">Schrodinger's Cat</a>: until someone checks to see if the door is there or not, it's in an indeterminate state where it may or may not be there, as far as the Talent is concerned: one might say that its existence is in Flux. And not only does the Talent get to treat it as being in Flux, he gets to determine (subconsciously) how that Flux will resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I got that, indeed, that was my first thought. The problem is: the construction workers that built - or not built - that door already know if it exists. The Talent doesn't, but a lot of in-universe people <i>do</i>. And these people &quot;opened the box&quot; at the moment they knew if the cat was dead or alive.<br /> <br /> TC Core says you can use Dramatic Edit to make an antagonist society of NPCs suddenly be revealed to be a good organization, just pretending to be evil for years as a long-term strategy. In this case, Schroedinger's box was opened years ago, since said characters <i>knew they were undercover agents for years, </i>pretending to be evil. So, this explanation can't really stand on its own: if this explanation is correct, whenever a Talent tried to use Dramatic Edit (let's call it DE), he almost never would succeed, because <i>someone </i>would &quot;have opened the box&quot; before. It's quite difficult to imagine a situation without even a single one prior observer... :/<br /> <br /> &quot;-Oh, I use DE to find a gun in his drawer.&quot; -&gt; couldn't do it; the gun owner knows if he already put the gun there or not.<br /> &quot;-I use DE to find a manhole that probably wouldn't exist so I can escape&quot;. -&gt; couldn't do it; the workers of said manhole (or street) already know if it exists or not.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Schroedinger's box (or superposition, to be mor precise), doesn't work for DE. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:21:36-07:00","id":1451384,"title":"","content":"For Dramatic Editing purposes, only those capable of Dramatic Editing count as observers. So the guys who did or didn't build the door <i>are</i> the cat in the box: they're in the Flux that the Inspired observer is resolving; and the way it resolves determines whether or not they built the door. <br /> <br /> Now, if your Inspired character happens to hear one of them talking about how they didn't build a door there, this is going to subconsciously bias him against the possibility that there's a door there, which will make it harder for him to resolve the Flux in favor of the door being there. Harder, but not impossible: it could be that the construction workers were lying for some reason. But it's entirely <i>his</i> observation that will determine whether or not the door is there; the construction workers, not being Inspired, have no say in it.<br /> <br /> The limitations on this are two-fold: first, the Talent has no conscious control over it, and his subconscious expectations will influence how things are resolved. Second, there's the matter of consistency: once something has been established one way or the other, you cannot contradict it. For instance, once you've resolved the existence of the door as being there, you can't then decide that it <i>isn't</i> there. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Mind you, this only works on a meta-level so long as all of the players are playing characters capable of Dramatic Editing. Something like the issue you're describing becomes problematic in, say, an Aberrant-age game where one of the protagonists is a Talent and the rest are Novas, or an \u00c6on-era game with one Talent, two baselines, and a couple of psions: saying that the rest of them are \u201ccats in the box\u201d doesn't work, because it takes agency away from other players. But then, that's why I don't like the notion that Dramatic Editing is an in-setting phenomenon that applies solely to Talents; I prefer the more meta notion that it's a genre convention that only applies to the protagonists and other comparatively significant characters like the major antagonists, whether or not they're Inspired. <br /> <br /> But even under that view of things, the construction workers are extras, and <i>still</i> don't count as observers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-08-2021, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:08:44-07:00","id":1452060,"title":"","content":"Interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:16:40-07:00","id":1452659,"title":"","content":"If I understand multiverse theory\u2019s alternate times lines are the same things as alternate universes. Every time there is a possibility of more than one outcome you get a alternate timeline/universe the further bad the more divergent. Example a universe where the the dinosaurs didn\u2019t die isn\u2019t so much a alternate universe as much as a alternate timeline. Even in worlds where the laws of physics are different I.e. a world with magic is just a alternate timeline created durning the Big Bang. The problem is the further back the change the harder to reach. Most talents can only access the closest alternate\u2019s Mercer can access a greater range. If Mercer ascends or other talents do they would probably be able to travel all of the alternate time lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:48:15-07:00","id":1452662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1452659#post1452659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand multiverse theory\u2019s alternate times lines are the same things as alternate universes. Every time there is a possibility of more than one outcome you get a alternate timeline/universe the further bad the more divergent. Example a universe where the the dinosaurs didn\u2019t die isn\u2019t so much a alternate universe as much as a alternate timeline. Even in worlds where the laws of physics are different I.e. a world with magic is just a alternate timeline created durning the Big Bang. The problem is the further back the change the harder to reach. Most talents can only access the closest alternate\u2019s Mercer can access a greater range. If Mercer ascends or other talents do they would probably be able to travel all of the alternate time lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically you\u2019re correct. Though a timeline that diverged so far back that the laws of physics are different would be functionally indistinguishable from a totally alternate universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:58:34-07:00","id":1452665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451129-the-relations-of-flux-and-time?p=1452662#post1452662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically you\u2019re correct. Though a timeline that diverged so far back that the laws of physics are different would be functionally indistinguishable from a totally alternate universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was his point. <br /> <br /> My pushback on it is, what about universes that didn't branch out of the Big Bang? And who says that different timelines branching out from the Big Bang would have different physics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T12:21:17-07:00","id":1452669,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Good point. But any universe which includes planet Earth almost certainly diverged from the main timeline at some point.<br /> <br /> I did a headcanon thing where Divis Mal basically created a replica of the D&amp;D multiverse, complete with spelljamming and Planescape stuff and even a world called Gothic Earth (one of the more obscure Ravenloft settings I found on DTRPG). I did this cause there\u2019s no way a universe like that could ever arise as an alternate timeline. But I never actually used it when I played, and I\u2019m thinking about retconning it out of existence after reading some of the new TC stuff.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: I can see both your points, and the distinction is unlikely to matter to your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T14:53:22-07:00","id":1452698,"title":"","content":"There is a interesting book for the old Alternity called Tangents. It has a nice and very descriptive way to divide the different tangents (parallel realities) by the time they split and how different they are from our world.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have the book here, but there were 4 kinds of tangents, those that have political changes (that guy name is Paul and not John, Nazis won WWII, Roman Empire never fall, etc), those that have biological changes (dominant species are descendent of dinosaurs, there are 3 different human species), those that have geological differences (Earth is a snow planet, Earth doesn\u2019t exist, etc), and those that have a physical law changes (magic exists, the universe is hyperbolical, Earth is an self contained finite plane, etc).<br /> <br /> Worth reading for the ideas...<br /> <br /> Also, are you watching Loki? Big thing this multiverse ideas and Variants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T16:40:13-07:00","id":1452713,"title":"","content":"The point is that the changes that Talents deals with rarely rise to the level of any of those. They're things like \u201cthe bullet hits three inches to the left\u201d \u2014 stuff that's unlikely to have such a sweeping impact barring the Butterfly Effect. <br /> <br /> And again, \u201cparallels universes\u201d gives the impression of a discrete set of universes; whereas Ian's \u201cchance is a distortion of the timeline\u201d explanation operates on a continuum \u2014 more like a spectrum of colors. Between any two possible timelines, there's always an infinitude of interim timelines where the differences are more marginal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T17:19:31-07:00","id":1452720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div cla